nt dealing damage and  Frostbite without even costing you FP  when this is really great however is  when you use this R2 while fainting the  icicle attack doesn't have a huge range  so you can faint at a sort of middle  distance and actually make use of the  back step in kiting enemies around which  is a really awesome play style and I  wish Eldon ring had more techniques like  this these are the sort of little combat  intricacies that I love making build out  of and I have another really good tip  that spellcasters will appreciate so you  would have noticed that spells have a  set cast time right sorcery is like  carrion slicer have a wind-up before you  attack as do incantations like Stone of  grunk however one really cool thing is  you can make a lot of these spells come  out a lot faster if you combo them with  other spells and attacks for example you  can remove the wind up on carrion slicer  if you cast it right after a regular  melee attack or cast it right after  casting a different spell here's a  comparison  as for incantations magma breath comes  out way faster if you use catch flame  right before it which actually goes a  really long way to making magma breath a  viable spell there are a ton of other  spells that work this way and while the  inputs can be a little bit tricky with  the d-pad it's a really fun high skill  cap thing that you can do to deepen the  gameplay of your spellcaster there are a  lot of spells that combo in this way I'm  gonna write my ones that I know in a  pinned comment down below so reply to  that with your own if you know of any  that I've missed now doing this makes  spell casting a bit more of a high skill  cap thing but if you want to make  spellcasting less complicated well I  have just the thing for you defeat radan  and progress below Lim grave here to  find the mimic tier ashes in nocron  everyone knows this summon is powerful  at this point how could it not be it's  just a copy of everything on your  character at the point point it is  summoned even your talismans and  speaking of talismans there's a Talisman  in the game called shabri's woe which  you can find here in the frenzied  Village when it's equipped this Talisman  forces enemies to focus their attacks on  you to the point that they'll actually  ignore your summons completely usually  this kind of just makes the game more  dangerous for you especially during  Co-op but one clever thing that you can  do with this Talisman is to have it  equipped and then summon your mimic tier  and then take shibiri's woe off your  character so since your mimic tear was  summoned with this Talisman equipped it  will now take all of the enemy aggro  leaving you free to cast ranged attacks  with complete impunity this is a really  good way to help increase the viability  of bow builds for example but it's also  a great way to make sorcery completely  broken since sorcery is very powerful  you could even go a step further with  this and give your mimic a great Shield  before you unlock equip it yourself so  if you really want them to tank for you  then this is what you do of course all  of you know about armor alteration at  this point but there are three  surprising facts about armor alteration  that I think a lot of people might have  missed first altering a piece of armor  affects its stats in all cases that I  could find altered versions of armor  offer less resistances but are lower  weight as well so if you're just shy of  having the right equip load consider  altering a few pieces of armor fashion  is important yes but not if it means fat  rolling next in some cases altering your  armor can give it special properties or  take them away the altered duelist cloak  for example reveals its snakes which are  this reviled symbol that makes enemies  Focus their attacks on you as if you  were wearing the shabri's woe Talisman  that I mentioned before as another  example altering the black knife chest  piece removes its concealing Veil which  naturally also removes its stealth  enhancing capabilities if you have any  other examples like this let me know in  the comments and finally and most  importantly for me a lot of altered  armor sets have different lore  descriptions the altered land of Reed's  armor for example tells you more about  the actual land of reeds which is locked  in a miserable Civil War during which  time it has remained alienated from the  cultures of its neighbors  as another example the altered version  of Loretta's Royal Knight armor has a  different description that describes her  Endeavors after she stopped being a  carrion Knight and fittingly the altered  armor set has the carrion colors removed  so yes it makes sense that this armor  with them removed would describe a  different point in this night's life  there are a ton of altered armor sets  that work this way and I just think this  is such an amazing little detail for the  devs to have included but one thing that  I kind of wish that they didn't include  are these chariots they suck that said  the difficulty that you have getting  past these chariots kind of makes  destroying them feel even better and if  you do manage to destroy them you get  really good rewards the first Chariot  you can encounter is behind a stone  sword door in The Fringe folk Hero's  grave back where you started the game so  let's destroy it to do this carefully  make your way past the chariot dropping  down at pretty much every ledge that you  see until you end up at a poison swamp  then take the elevator back up here  you'll have a line of fire to these  giant pots that hang above the roof  hidden in the shadows and when they drop  they explode in Blue Flame so line up a  shot wait for the Chariot to bump into  the wall below you and that is your  trigger to fire you get three attempts  at this there are three pots and when  you do drop it it explodes The Chariot  giving you the odd tree great bow in  return this bow does extra damage with  wholly infused arrows and it scales with  faith as well the next set of Chariots  are in the oritsa hero's grave here  there's a section with two chariots and  we need to destroy these two so to do  that we need to introduce a third  Chariot into the mix to do this run down  to the point right before the locked  door where a third Chariot spawns and  comes towards you use this corpse on the  edge as a guide to drop down further to  some Rafters continue further down in  this direction until you find another  Chariot ramp at this point you can go  further up or down the ramp both will  lead you to this same pillar of imp  statues that breathe fire make sure you  hit it once just once to send it upwards  this pillar also includes the Roses  statue that summons the Chariots and  this will send a chariot spawn further  up to crash so head back up die if you  need to and watch them crash you'll  receive the tree Sentinel armor set and  the Holy Ground Ash of War for your  efforts in galmir Hero's grave you can't  destroy the riderless Chariot but you  can become its Rider to do this you jump  down into the Gap make sure you jump  into this corner here you'll land on the  Rafters and from these Rafters you can  jump down onto the riderless Chariot but  before you do that go inside the window  to loot the gelmere set and killed the  Bloodhound that's two rare armor sets  already which is great then go back to  the rafters and drop down onto the  riderless Chariot this way you'll go  even further down into the lava and  you'll finish the dungeon as a reward  alternatively though you can backstep  down through this lava or Quick Step  through but that's kind of a lot less  fun for number nine did you know that  weather can affect your damage if it's  raining you'll do around 10 percent less  fire damage but your lightning damage  will be increased by 10 in my testing it  was around 10 and these effects even  applied to enemies that were undercover  from the rain so I guess that suggests  that this effect is applied to  everything in an area not just every  enemy that's wet per se this rain effect  is something you should really keep in  mind if you're doing Jewels at the main  Academy gate in Raya lucaria this is  where people do Jewels By the way it  seems to rain really often in Leonia and  Light builds will inherently be at an  advantage here I guess while fire builds  will be at a disadvantage lastly let's  talk about buff stacking that's a great  way to get an advantage sort of  regardless of your build as well  so disregarding Talisman and armor Buffs  which are permanent there are different  categories of temporary Buffs in Olden  ring and you can only have one temporary  buff active from each category there are  weapon Buffs Shield Buffs body Buffs  Aura Buffs health regen Buffs and  stamina regen Buffs and in addition to  these there are some special Buffs that  don't follow any of these rules so keep  those in mind that's Holy Ground and  Terra Magica for example now activating  as many temporary Buffs as you can is a  huge way to unlock the potential of your  character so here are the Buffs that  I've found that basically work on every  character to start you can activate  health and stamina regen Buffs just with  your flask of wondrous physic you just  need the Crimson burst tier and the  green burst tier these tiers are located  here and here next an easy way to get  access to an aura buff is the golden  vowel Ash War which is located here this  gives you 15 extra damage and 15 damage  negation as well and you can just put  this on a light dagger you can activate  it and then switch back to your main  weapon that's incredible as for body  Buffs The Black Guard sells infinite  boiled crab here and then here which  gives you 20 extra physical resistance  and as for weapon and shield Buffs these  kind of do depend on your build if your  armaments can be infused you should  absolutely be trying to use something  from this list  before I